            {"category": "HR", "difficulty": "easy", "question_type": "hr_general", "question_text": "Why do you want to work at Wipro, and what values from the 'Spirit of Wipro' resonate with you most?", "sample_answer": "The Spirit of Wipro emphasizes 'Be passionate about clients' success, treat each person with respect, and unyielding integrity'. These principles match my personal work ethic and desire to grow in a value-driven global organization."},
            {"category": "HR", "difficulty": "easy", "question_type": "hr_general", "question_text": "Are you comfortable working on legacy modernization projects (e.g., maintaining established enterprise code) as well as new technologies?", "sample_answer": "Yes. Understanding enterprise legacy codebases teaches critical domain logic and architecture patterns that are invaluable when modernizing systems."},
            {"category": "Technical", "difficulty": "easy", "question_type": "technical_basics", "question_text": "What is polymorphism in Object-Oriented Programming? Give a real-world example.", "sample_answer": "Polymorphism means 'many forms'. It allows entities to take on different behaviors. For example, a base class 'PaymentMethod' has a method 'pay()'. Subclasses 'CreditCardPayment' and 'UPIPayment' execute distinct payment logic through the same interface."},
            {"category": "Technical", "difficulty": "easy", "question_type": "technical_depth", "question_text": "Write or explain the logic to detect a loop in a Singly Linked List using Floyd's Cycle Detection algorithm.", "sample_answer": "Initialize two pointers: slow and fast, both starting at head. Traverse list: slow advances by 1 node, fast by 2 nodes. If fast or fast.next reaches null, no loop exists. If slow and fast pointers meet at the same node, a cycle is detected in O(N) time and O(1) space."}
