            {"category": "Technical", "difficulty": "medium", "question_type": "technical_depth", "question_text": "What is the difference between synchronous blocking I/O and asynchronous non-blocking I/O (e.g. Node.js or Spring WebFlux)?", "sample_answer": "Blocking I/O allocates one thread per request, blocking the thread while waiting for disk or network I/O. Non-blocking I/O uses an event loop with epoll/kqueue, handling thousands of concurrent connections with a small, fixed thread pool."},
